                          "String": "/LABORATORY ANIMALS: Acute Exposure/ Octanoate was found to stimulate the muscle proteins catabolism in rats with portacaval anastomosis thus increasing the amounts of 3-methylhistidine, creatinine, ammonium and urea in the excreted urine. The intensive decomposition of the endogenous proteins also produced great amounts of HCO3- whose levels increased in both the urine and blood. It is suggested that in hepatic insufficiency octanoate causes metabolic acidosis through: a) more intensive catabolism of the muscle proteins whose decomposition results in greater amounts of HCO3-, b) metabolization of octanoate to HCO3-, and c) inhibition of the ornithine cycle.",
