                      "StringWithMarkup": [
                        {
                          "String": "Octanoic acid was detected in trench leachate from low-level radioactive waste disposal sites in Maxey Flats, KY and West Valley, NY at an average concn of 0.83 and 15 mg/L, respectively(1). Octanoic acid was detected in process retort water from the Occidental Oil Shale, Inc facility in Logan Wash, CO at a concn of 131 mg/L(2). Octanoic acid was detected in: product water samples from an in situ coal gasification site in Hanna, WY at a concn of 110 ppm; retort water from in situ oil shale processing in Rock Springs, WY at a concn of 14 ppm; and boiler blowdown water from in situ shale oil processing in DeBeque, CO at a concn of 115 ppm(3). Octanoic acid was found at 1043.0 ug/g from heated roofing tar pot fumes(4). Octanoic acid was found at 29,400 and 9,290 ug/kg in the gas and particulate matter from charbroiling meat(5). Octanoic acid was identified as a fine particle released from a natural gas-fired space heater and water heater; emission rates were 152.0 pg/kJ and 116.9 pg/kJ for the first series of filters and backup filters within the samplers, respectively(6). Octanoic acid was detected in emissions from a municipal waste incineration plant at a concn of 0.28 ug/cu m(7). Aerosol emission rates of octanoic acid from frying hamburger meat was 4.1 mg/kg of meat cooked; emission rates from charbroiling hamburger was 14.8 mg/kg of meat cooked for extra lean hamburger (approx. 10.0% fat) and 25.2 mg/kg of meat cooked for regular hamburger (approx. 21% fat)(8).",
